From 01a0d18bda9242c416220b435d832a1731448718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:23:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Contacts: add static paper-ink presentation

Upstream colours nothing reads keep their upstream values (action_bar_background, call_arrow_green/red, snackbar_background, search_video_call_icon_tint, device_account_tint_color, disabled_button_background/text, control_highlight_color, contacts_accent_color, drawer_selected_color, nav_item_selected_background).

Rows and borderless targets (theme selectable/list/action-bar backgrounds, list items, drawer items) have no frame at rest, so adjacent views no longer double their edges; the search back arrow is ink (was white on white); the call-with-a-note card and subject list, the navigation drawer (1px end line) and the empty-state buttons (outlined pills, no recolouring filter) are outlined; QuickContact cards use a 28dp edge matching their clip; white letter tiles get a whole-pixel ink ring.

Row, control and FAB focus edges are whole-pixel 1dp (2px at 300dpi) and active states one 2dp edge instead of a second inset ring; dashes are 3dp/2dp. Dialog windows (contacts_eink_window, dialog_background) and popup menus (white native nine-patch) have no drawable stroke, so the window border (FlatWindowBorder) draws their only edge. Progress rings are round(density) wide; the drawer keeps its 1px end line.
